# ── PM-GROOM LANE (BH-7261, BH-7244.3) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Monday 11:0x UTC, two hours after run-product: the PM agent's weekly
# grooming brief per product project. It reads the roadmap backlog and the
# newest data-signals.json, claims the (project, week) brief row BEFORE its one
# model call (role product.pm), stores the brief and its proposed moves, and
# sends a Telegram text with Mission Control links. It shares the run-product
# flock (flock -n: a held lock is a skip). It never posts or builds.
# Off: flags/lane-off-pm-groom, or bin/harness-ctl.sh off pm-groom.
# @box project-4
8 11 * * 1 /root/harness/bin/pm-groom.sh project-4 >> /root/harness/logs/pm-groom.log 2>&1
# @box project-1
2 11 * * 1 /root/harness/bin/pm-groom.sh project-1 >> /root/harness/logs/pm-groom.log 2>&1
# @box project-2
4 11 * * 1 /root/harness/bin/pm-groom.sh project-2 >> /root/harness/logs/pm-groom.log 2>&1
# @box project-3
6 11 * * 1 /root/harness/bin/pm-groom.sh project-3 >> /root/harness/logs/pm-groom.log 2>&1
# @box project-9
5 11 * * 1 /root/harness/bin/pm-groom.sh project-9 >> /root/harness/logs/pm-groom.log 2>&1
# @box project-5
9 11 * * 1 /root/harness/bin/pm-groom.sh project-5 >> /root/harness/logs/pm-groom.log 2>&1
# @box small
1 11 * * 1 /root/harness/bin/pm-groom.sh project-8 >> /root/harness/logs/pm-groom.log 2>&1
# @box project-6-os
1 11 * * 1 /root/harness/bin/pm-groom.sh project-6-os >> /root/harness/logs/pm-groom.log 2>&1
